pySMESH: make StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D stop on a cancel again (SMESH V9_16_0).

Symptom: a cancel (SMESH_Gen::CancelCompute, or a progress hook that cancels) no longer
stops Cartesian_3D. The algorithm runs to its end, and only then does the compute report the
cancel. A cancelled run keeps the complete mesh and takes longer than a run without a cancel.

Upstream commit: SMESH 9f7d4a55e (2024-05-26, bos #42002, "Bodyfitting refactoring") moved
the grid steps of StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D::Compute into
Cartesian3D::Grid::GridInitAndInterserctWithShape.

Root cause: Compute passes the member flag _computeCanceled (volatile bool, SMESH_Algo.hxx)
by value. The three checks in the grid function (after SetCoordinates, after the
intersection, after ComputeNodes) test a copy taken at the call, so they never see a cancel
that arrives later. Compute also ignores the bool that the function returns. V9_9_0 tested
the member itself at the same three points of Compute, and returned false.

Change (the cancel path only; a run without a cancel builds the same mesh):
* StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D_Grid.hxx and .cxx, Grid::GridInitAndInterserctWithShape: take the
  flag as volatile bool&, so that each of the three checks reads the live member.
* StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx, StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D::Compute: return false when the grid
  function returns false. It returns false only at its three cancel checks.

Not changed: StdMeshers.test/HexahedronTest.cxx and HexahedronCanonicalShapesTest.cxx pass a
literal false; pySMESH does not build them. Hexahedron::MakeElements (the threaded volume
step) has no cancel check, the same as in V9_9_0. With a ViscousLayers hypothesis, Compute
builds the offset shape, then calls itself; the inner call resets the flag at its start (as
V9_9_0's Compute did), so a cancel during the offset step is lost, and the layer step has no
check. Upstream master at 83f8bf482 (2026-09-14) still passes the flag by value.

diff --git a/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx b/src/StdMeshers/StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx
index 5a88d03..74730fe 100644
